{
  _type: 'element',
  tags: null,
  links: null,
  _stage: 'layouted',
  sourcePath: 'views.c4',
  description: {
    txt: 'Six systems, each named for the responsibility it owns. Networking is the session boundary above Messaging: it owns Client/Server roles, peer admission, liveness and logical routing, while Messaging owns links, routes, channels, serialization and reliable delivery. Engine owns optional Messaging and Networking and gives each World a non-owning Network pointer. Networking never sees a device or endpoint; Transport never sees Networking, Messaging or Engine. Messaging and Transport meet only at the Core transport-device interface, and the application composition root registers concrete devices and advances each exactly once. Direct Messaging and direct Transport remain independently usable.',
  },
  title: '[C2] MicroWorld',
  id: 'c2Systems',
  autoLayout: {
    direction: 'TB',
  },
