      description: {
        txt: 'Delivers named messages through channels, with or without a device.',
      },
      tags: [],
      metadata: {
        contract: 'FMessagingSystem: fixed links, explicit routes, named channels, subscriptions, frame codecs and bounded reliable delivery. FMessage carries a name id, bounded payload and local-only source metadata',
        standalone: 'Usable with no transport at all: a local-only channel delivers only to this node. Direct Messaging may also use a known default route without Networking',
        boundary: 'It reaches bytes only through the transport device interface in Core, so no medium is named here and no message type is named in Transport. Delivery guarantees live here, per channel and complete route, because Transport answers acceptance and never delivery. Networking consumes Messaging channels and explicit routes; Messaging does not own peers or roles',
      },
      technology: '[system: engine service]',
